Z||000002||frontal lobe||03-14-2001||02:38 PM||||One of the best middle linebackers the NFL has ever witnessed, he played in several championships with the Lombardi-led Packers of the 1960's.  A graduate of the U. of Illinois, he was known for being as gentle off the field as ferocious on.  He passed away a few years ago.<P>I don't know a LOT about his philosophy, but I know it involved gang-tackling, getting penetration into the backfield, etc.  Hope that helps.||||reg||1
