Z||000004||Will||03-15-2001||09:39 AM||||"That which does not kill us only makes us stronger."<P>But I like<P>"Crush your enemies, see them driven before you, and hear the lamentations of their women."||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||03-15-2001||06:52 PM||||Believe it or not, I have.  I own several of his books and still read his stuff on occasion.  There is hardly anything he says in his books that isn't contradicted by himself somewhere else.  Lets see.... His health was poor.  He would write and write and write until he literally couldn't SEE anymore.  He spent some time in the military and suffered injuries that allowed him to go home.  He taught at a University in Germany.  Towards the end of his life he became mentally unstable.  This is strange... Some believe that he contracted siphyllis(sp?) from a prostitute and it eventually led to his demise.  He's EXTREMELY quotable.  It seems that almost every page of his books has at least one good quote.  Check out "the portable nietzche"  It's a really cool book.  There's lots and lots of cool facts about him.||||reg||1
